/*
  ============================================================
  CODE 3 MX7000 - GIGA DISPLAY CONTROLLER
  Arduino GIGA R1 WiFi + GIGA Display Shield
  ============================================================

  GIGA <-> NANO ESP32 UART
  -----------------------
  GIGA D1 TX  -> Nano D12 RX
  GIGA D0 RX  <- Nano D13 TX
  GIGA GND    -> Nano GND
  Baud: 38400


  ============================================================
  LIGHTBAR BUTTON COLORS
  ============================================================

  DARK
    Inactive

  BLUE
    Physical switch active

  FLASHING BLUE
    Physical switch active but in 120-second startup hold

  RED
    Physical switch is ON but GIGA override is inhibiting it

  FLASHING PURPLE
    GIGA START/STOP command is waiting for confirmation

  SOLID PURPLE
    GIGA START/STOP command failed to confirm after 30 seconds

  GREEN
    GIGA START command confirmed by Mega


  ============================================================
  PHYSICAL OVERRIDE
  ============================================================

  BLUE BUTTON:
    Hold approximately 2 seconds
    -> OVERRIDE <COMMAND> ON

  FLASHING BLUE BUTTON:
    Hold approximately 2 seconds
    -> OVERRIDE <COMMAND> ON
    -> prevents output from starting when startup hold expires

  RED BUTTON:
    Hold approximately 2 seconds
    -> OVERRIDE <COMMAND> OFF
    -> physical switch regains control

  PHYSICAL SWITCH TURNED OFF:
    Nano should automatically clear the override.
    GIGA then receives P=0 O=0 and button becomes DARK.


  ============================================================
  NORMAL GIGA COMMAND RETRIES
  ============================================================

  0 sec   Send command
          Flash purple

  5 sec   Retry

  10 sec  Retry

  15 sec  Retry

  20 sec  Retry

  25 sec  Retry

  30 sec  Give up
          Solid purple

  CONFIRMED at any point immediately ends retrying.


  ============================================================
  COMMUNICATION STATUS
  ============================================================

  NANO OK:
    Any complete received Nano message within timeout.

  NANO LOST:
    No complete Nano message within timeout.

  MEGA OK:
    Recent verified forwarded Mega PONG / link restored
    AND Nano itself is still reachable.

  MEGA LOST:
    No recent Mega verification OR Nano is LOST.

  Link status is calculated directly from timestamps.
  There are no persistent nanoLinkLost / megaLinkLost flags.
  ============================================================
*/


